DERIVATIVE WORK
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  Project      : InterfaceTester
  Version      : 5.0.1
  License      : Apache License, Version 2.0 (see LICENSE)
  Maintainer   : honky212

  This repository is an independently maintained fork. It is a *modified* version
  of the upstream Work. In accordance with Section 4(b) of the Apache License 2.0,
  notice is hereby given that the files in this repository HAVE BEEN CHANGED from
  the upstream Work.

  Principal changes introduced by this fork include, but are not limited to:

    1. Package and command renaming. The Python package is named "interfacetester"
       and the console entry points are "hrun", "hmake", "hconvert", and
       "interfacetester". Upstream module and CLI naming has been adapted
       accordingly.

    2. Build system migration. The upstream Poetry-based build backend was replaced
       with a setuptools backend (PEP 621 + PEP 639) in pyproject.toml.

    3. Correctness hardening ("false pass" prevention). Numerous validation gates
       were added at generation time and runtime so that a test case cannot pass
       while silently validating nothing. Examples include duplicate YAML key
       rejection, assertion operator whitelisting, inline JSON Schema rejection,
       XSD path existence checks, request body ambiguity gates, and step-type
       mutual exclusion.

    4. Reporting and observability fixes. Failed steps are now recorded in
       summaries; configuration-stage failures are reported as failures rather
       than successes; misleading record fields (for example, content_size) were
       corrected.

    5. Security and credential handling. A whitelist was introduced for Python
       builtins usable in "${...}" interpolation; sensitive values are masked in
       logs, reports, and summary artifacts; multipart header parameters are
       escaped.

    6. XML/SOAP support. Built-in "xpath_match", "xpath_count", and
       "xml_schema_match" assertion operators were added (optional "xml" extra),
       plus a zero-dependency project-level fallback.

    7. Importers. A "hconvert" command was added to convert curl, HAR, Postman,
       and OpenAPI assets into standard YAML test cases.

    8. Additional comparators and built-in functions, test data management
       conventions, and CI templates were added.

  For the complete and authoritative list of modifications, consult the
  repository history and documentation, in particular README.md and
  docs/架构与调用链.md. This list is informational and is not exhaustive.

